module gunbc.rung_drop.concat_binary_signature_exempt_from_arg_binding

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing }

data concat_binary_signature_exempt_from_arg_binding: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "concat_binary_signature_exempt_from_arg_binding" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "n-ary concat call sites judged against concat's binary declared signature",

  declared: "2026-09-01",

  standing: Standing,

  authored: "Builtin signature grounding -- **RUNG DROP, DECLARED (2026-09-01).** PREVIOUS RUNG: none to lower -- nothing binds builtin arguments today, so this declares a class that the arm flip would otherwise create. concat's declared signature is BINARY, and it is binary correctly: std.algebra declares param_types [ReceiverSelf, ReceiverSelf], and src/v1/runtime_rust.dag emits `pub fn concat<T: V2Concat>(a: T, b: T) -> T`. The algebra and the emitted runtime agree; only the CORPUS calls concat at other arities. TEMPORARY RUNG: mitigatable. concat is exempted from the direct-call argument-shape judgement when decide_callable_candidates begins answering FuncSigResolved for a BuiltinCallable; every other builtin is judged. REASON: concat(a, b, c) is a FOLD of the binary associative operation, and what licenses folding an n-ary application into nested binary applications is ASSOCIATIVITY, which is not modeled. std.algebra declares Magma<T> as { op: fn(T, T) -> T } and Semigroup<T> as { op: fn(T, T) -> T } -- structurally identical, differing by a blank line where the law would sit. The type whose entire content is the associativity law carries no law, so nothing in the tree can say an operation is associative, and the missing capability is one level below the signature rather than in it. Widening AlgebraTypeTemplate with a variadic arm was refused because variadicity is not a property of a parameter's TYPE -- that vocabulary answers what type a position has, not how many positions there are -- and DESIGN section 4 puts surface arity in the sugar layer that adds no power. Declaring concat's signature absent was refused because the signature is expressible and true; erasing a fact that holds is a different failure from asserting one that does not. POPULATION: measured over dag, src/v1 and src/v2 with a scanner that skips string literals -- 12 free-call sites at arity 1, 8297 at 2, 507 at 3, 200 at 4, 178 at 5, and a tail to 262, across 64 distinct arities, roughly 1200 sites above binary. Closes by re-measurement, not by opinion. RESTORATION TRIGGER: n-ary application of a binary operation DECLARED ASSOCIATIVE folds to nested binary application -- SUFFICIENT FOR accepting concat's 64 measured arities against its unchanged binary declared signature, with no exemption and no widened vocabulary. Its own prerequisite is that associativity be declarable at all, which today it is not; that grounding is a DESIGN section 5 wall-after-grounding rather than a ratchet, since associativity of a declared operation is a modeled fact and not an undecidable one."
}
